<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>HTML5 Links &amp; Attributes</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.6;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 20px auto;
            padding: 0 16px;
        }
        .spacer {
            height: 550px;
            background-color: #f8fafc;
            border: 1px dashed #cbd5e1;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        img {
            border-radius: 8px;
            border: 2px solid #0284c7;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body id="top">

    <h1>HTML5 Link Types &amp; Attributes</h1>

    <!-- 1. INTERNAL LINKS -->
    <h2>1. Internal Links</h2>
    <ul>
        <!-- Fragment / Same-Page Anchor Link -->
        <li>
            <a href="#bottom-section" title="Scroll down to the footer section">
                Jump to Bottom Section (Same-Page Anchor)
            </a>
        </li>

        <!-- Relative Path to Another Local HTML File -->
        <li>
            <a href="timetable.html" title="Open local timetable page">
                View Class Timetable (Local Relative File)
            </a>
        </li>

        <!-- Local File Download Link -->
        <li>
            <a href="syllabus.pdf" download="CS_Syllabus_2026.pdf" title="Download PDF file">
                Download Course Syllabus (<code>download</code> attribute)
            </a>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <hr>

    <!-- 2. EXTERNAL LINKS -->
    <h2>2. External Links</h2>
    <p>
        <!-- target="_blank" opens in a new tab; rel="noopener noreferrer" prevents tabnabbing -->
        Check your markup validity using the 
        <a href="https://validator.w3.org/" 
           target="_blank" 
           rel="noopener noreferrer" 
           title="Opens W3C Validator in a new browser tab">
           W3C Markup Validation Service
        </a>.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <!-- 3. EMAIL LINKS -->
    <h2>3. Email Links (<code>mailto:</code>)</h2>
    <ul>
        <!-- Basic Email Link -->
        <li>
            <a href="mailto:admissions@example.edu">
                Email Admissions Office (Basic)
            </a>
        </li>

        <!-- Email Link with Pre-filled Subject, CC, and Body -->
        <li>
            <a href="mailto:hod.cs@example.edu?cc=advisor@example.edu&subject=Lab%20Schedule%20Query&body=Respected%20Sir%2C%0A%0AI%20have%20a%20question%20regarding%20the%20timetable.">
                Email Department Head with Subject &amp; Body
            </a>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <hr>

    <!-- 4. IMAGE LINKS -->
    <h2>4. Image Links</h2>
    <p>Wrapping an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> inside an <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> tag turns the image into a clickable link:</p>

    <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML" 
       target="_blank" 
       rel="noopener noreferrer" 
       aria-label="Visit MDN HTML Documentation">
        <img src="https://picsum.photos/id/0/360/160" 
             alt="Laptop displaying web development workspace" 
             title="Click to open MDN HTML Documentation"
             width="360" 
             height="160">
    </a>

    <!-- Spacer box to demonstrate same-page vertical jumping -->
    <div class="spacer">
        <p><em>Scroll down or click "Jump to Bottom Section" above to test the internal anchor link...</em></p>
    </div>

    <!-- TARGET ELEMENT FOR SAME-PAGE ANCHOR -->
    <footer id="bottom-section">
        <h3>Bottom Section (<code>id="bottom-section"</code>)</h3>
        <p>You navigated directly to this section using <code>href="#bottom-section"</code>.</p>
        <p><a href="#top">&uarr; Back to Top</a></p>
    </footer>

</body>

